--- !u!114 &187848943
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 187848941}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b58ee1c4ed8bd1542be3e660daf4b8fc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PPTManager
  pages:
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bd45076969a8e0a45aa50c3bdbd60da8, type: 3}
    description: 'Jump King''s goal is simple: keep climbing. But one badly timed
      jump can send you falling a very long way. You don''t die, but you can lose
      a huge amount of progress. And then you have to climb all the way back.

'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ca37f1395951cdd4b9c3d10da9d81841, type: 3}
    description: 'I have a friend named Harry. He loves games that make him suffer,
      sometimes playing them for an entire day. One morning, he told me how difficult
      Jump King was and insisted that I give it a try.

'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e9953244c11719a4dab6dcd96864b4ba, type: 3}
    description: 'After a few failed jumps, I understood exactly what he meant. I
      immediately gave the game back to him. But when I saw Harry again near evening,
      he was still playing. Still jumping. Still trying to climb higher.

'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7b7f29f7a9928a44e9016a29ef548bc5, type: 3}
    description: 'Then I had an idea. If the whole point of Jump King is to keep
      going higher, why not just give him a jetpack? In my dream, there''s no need
      to master those frustrating jumps. Just fly straight to the top.

'
  - image: {fileID: 0}
    description: "WASD \u2014 Move\r\n"
  picture: {fileID: 818537747}
  text: {fileID: 348342826}
