'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d3e61ff3abff05e4dae8bd7edf07e48f, type: 3}
    description: 'Outside my high school classroom, there was a touchscreen that
      seemed to be used for school management. Somehow, it had Flappy Bird installed
      on it.

'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: fc177fdf9e6316142808ea3967979131, type: 3}
    description: 'The touchscreen reacted with a noticeable delay. The bird kept
      hitting pipes, and getting past even ten was difficult. I still played outside
      the classroom for ages.

'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ea7d7a5e3763d9a4f9d267a72943a0c2, type: 3}
    description: "One day, my homeroom teacher caught me gaming and got furious.
      Our school could confiscate students' computers\u2014but this screen belonged
      to the school. She couldn't take it away, so she scolded me instead.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 0}
    description: "The lag made every attempt frustrating. After all those failures\u2014and
      that lecture from my teacher\u2014I never touched that school touchscreen again.\r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 0}
    description: 'In the original game, a tiny touch against a pipe meant instant
      death. But this is just a dream, the rules have changed. Now the bird can smash
      the pipes away.

'
  - image: {fileID: 0}
    description: "Space \u2014 Jump\r\n"
  picture: {fileID: 1273049733}
  text: {fileID: 97192387}
