--- !u!114 &1193526073
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1193526071}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b58ee1c4ed8bd1542be3e660daf4b8fc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PPTManager
  pages:
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b344e939404c69241926782387f4d64e, type: 3}
    description: 'Compared with the other games, Hotline Miami is a little more forgiving.
      Restarting after death is quick. But you still have to repeat rooms, learn
      enemy behavior, and react fast. One mistake can end your run instantly.

'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e0691342012af2140bc4ca2968bd5336, type: 3}
    description: 'There''s another problem: this game is exhausting to look at. The
      flashing colors and frantic action become tiring after a while. Some enemy
      behavior is unpredictable, too. And you keep replaying the same room.

'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e5d5dcdf0ac39fa42a47e5710c17184e, type: 3}
    description: 'A friend who absolutely loves violent action games recommended
      Hotline Miami to me. He enjoys the combat a little too much. Once, I watched
      him playing Warhammer 40,000: Space Marine 2, laughing wildly while cutting
      through enemies.

'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2ed1d16da542602468c4019130dedf16, type: 3}
    description: 'After a few hours, I couldn''t take it anymore. It was too difficult,
      and my eyes were exhausted. But my friend was completely different. He actually
      managed to finish both Hotline Miami games.

'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7e9bd3cb780155f4eae2649651810c14, type: 3}
    description: "In Hotline Miami, you can fight enemies with a baseball bat. But
      some enemies have guns, and one shot can kill you. So in my dream, I decided
      to give Jacket a ridiculously oversized bat. Touch an enemy, and they're instantly
      knocked out. \r\n"
  - image: {fileID: 0}
    description: "WASD \u2014 Move"
  picture: {fileID: 1007899250}
  text: {fileID: 804186823}
